/-!
# Descending an invertible module along a finite morphism

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a finite morphism of schemes, let `V : Y.Opens` be an open over which `f` is
an isomorphism, assume `Y \ V` is a discrete space, and let `L` be an invertible `𝒪_X`-module.
[Stacks, Tag 0C0T] asserts that `L` is the pullback of an invertible `𝒪_Y`-module. This file
constructs that module, proves it invertible, and identifies its pullback with `L`.

## The construction

[Stacks, Tag 0BUT], `Stacks.Divisors.hasTrivializingTargetCover_of_isFinite`, gives
every point `y` of `Y` an open neighbourhood over which `L` is trivial on the inverse image.
Shrinking that neighbourhood produces a cover of `Y` by opens `W y` with the extra property
that **two distinct charts meet only inside `V`**: for `y ∈ V` take the neighbourhood
intersected with `V`, and for `y ∉ V` use discreteness of the complement to find an open
meeting `Y \ V` only in `y`. That is `ChartData`.

The ratio of two chart generators of `L` therefore always lives over an open contained in `V`,
where `f` is an isomorphism and so `f.app` is invertible on sections — `isIso_app_of_le`. Each
such ratio consequently descends to a unit on the target (`descendUnit`), the descended units
inherit the restriction, inverse and cocycle laws, and `ChartData.transitionCocycle` packages
them as a `Stacks.SheafOfModules.UnitTransitionCocycle` on `Y`. Gluing that cocycle gives
`LiftedChartData.descend`, an invertible `𝒪_Y`-module.

On the diagonal `i = j` the chart need not lie in `V`, so the transition there is set to `1`
directly; the case split is harmless because a transition between *distinct* charts is always
over an open inside `V`, which is exactly `ChartData.eq_of_not_le`.

## The comparison with `L`, for transition units from any source

The comparison does not use the isomorphism over `V` at all. Its input is `LiftedChartData`: a
cover by charts with a generator of `L` over the inverse image of each, a unit cocycle on the
charts, and the single compatibility that **each transition unit pulls back to the ratio of the
two chart generators**. Tag 0C0T's chart data supplies one, `ChartData.toLiftedChartData`, and
that is the only place the isomorphism over `V` is used below, and only through the
invertibility of `f.app` over the opens inside `V`, `ChartData.toLiftedChartDataOfIsIsoApp`.
A *chosen* lift of the ratios serves equally well, which is what a closed immersion with
nilpotent ideal provides and what Tag 09NY needs.

A section of `LiftedChartData.descend` over `W` is a compatible family of coordinates
`s i ∈ Γ(𝒪_Y, W ⊓ chart i)` — the sections of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.UnitTransitionCocycle.sectionsSubmodule`. Over an open inside a single
chart the `i`-th coordinate carries all of that data
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.UnitTransitionCocycle.chartLinearEquiv`), and
`LiftedChartData.localSection` sends it to the section `f^#(s i) • σ i` of `L`, with `σ i` the
`i`-th chart generator. Two charts assign the same section,
`LiftedChartData.localSection_eq`, exactly because of the compatibility above. So
[Stacks, Tag 04TN] — `TopCat.Sheaf.existsUnique_hom_of_localHom` — glues the chart-local
assignments into a map of sheaves of sets, and additivity, semilinearity and naturality are
checked chart by chart against the sheaf condition. That is
`LiftedChartData.pushforwardComparison : descend ⟶ f_*L`, and
`LiftedChartData.pullbackComparison` is its adjunct under
`Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction`.

The adjunct is an isomorphism, `LiftedChartData.isIso_pullbackComparison`. The chart section
whose `i`-th coordinate is one is sent to the `i`-th chart generator,
`LiftedChartData.pushforwardComparison_chartSection`, so the adjunct is **surjective** on the
sections over every open inside `f⁻¹(chart i)`. The pullback `f^*(descend)` is invertible by
`Stacks.Modules.isInvertible_pullback`, so on a refinement of the chart cover both sides are
free of rank one, and a surjective map between modules each freely generated by one section is
bijective — it is multiplication by a scalar which surjectivity forces to be a unit. The sheaf
condition, `Stacks.SheafOfModules.bijective_app_of_bijective_on_cover`, propagates bijectivity
to every open. That argument is isolated as `bijective_app_of_generator_images`, for an
arbitrary morphism out of an invertible module, and no description of the sections of the
pullback functor is needed anywhere.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.PicFinite.descendUnitOfIsIsoApp`: a unit upstairs over an open inside `V`, descended
  to the target, for `f` invertible on the sections over every open inside `V`;
  `Stacks.PicFinite.descendUnit` is the case of an isomorphism over `V`.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.ChartData`: a cover of `Y` by trivializing charts meeting pairwise inside
  `V`, together with the chart generators of `L`.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.ChartData.transitionCocycle`: the descended transition units as gluing data.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.presheafHomOfFamily`: a morphism of presheaves of modules from a family of
  additive, semilinear maps compatible with restriction.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.typeSheafOfModules`: a sheaf of modules on a scheme read as a sheaf of sets.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.pull`: `f^#` on sections, as a ring map into the section ring in the
  spelling that acts on modules.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.LiftedChartData`: chart data together with a unit cocycle on the charts
  whose transitions pull back to the ratios of the chart generators — the input of the
  comparison, and all of it.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.ChartData.toLiftedChartDataOfIsIsoApp`: chart data, read as that input,
  for `f` invertible on the sections over every open inside `V`;
  `Stacks.PicFinite.ChartData.toLiftedChartData` is Tag 0C0T's case of an isomorphism over `V`.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.LiftedChartData.descend`: the glued `𝒪_Y`-module.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.LiftedChartData.chartGen`: a chart generator restricted to the preimage of a
  smaller open.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.LiftedChartData.localSection`: the section of `L` a compatible family of
  coordinates determines over an open inside one chart.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.LiftedChartData.pushforwardComparison` and
  `Stacks.PicFinite.LiftedChartData.pullbackComparison`: the comparison morphism and its
  adjunct.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.LiftedChartData.pullbackIso`: the adjunct as an isomorphism.

## Main results

* `Stacks.PicFinite.isIso_morphismRestrict_of_le` and `Stacks.PicFinite.isIso_app_of_le`: a
  morphism which is an isomorphism over `V` is one over every smaller open, and is then
  invertible on sections there.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.nonempty_chartData`: the chart data exist. This is where Tag 0BUT and the
  discreteness of the complement of `V` are used, and the only place.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.ChartData.pull_transition_val`: the descended transition unit pulls back to
  the ratio of the two chart generators. This is where the isomorphism over `V` is used.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.LiftedChartData.isInvertible_descend`: the glued module is invertible.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.bijective_app_of_generator_images`: a morphism out of an invertible module
  which hits a local generator over each member of an open cover is bijective on the sections
  over every open.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.LiftedChartData.localSection_eq`: the chart-local sections agree on
  overlaps.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.LiftedChartData.isIso_pullbackComparison`: the adjunct is an isomorphism.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.exists_isInvertible_modulePullback_iso`: **Tag 0C0T.**
* `Stacks.PicFinite.exists_isInvertible_modulePullback_iso_of_forall_isIso_app`:
  the same descent for any morphism invertible on the sections over every open inside `V`,
  given a trivializing cover of the target; finiteness enters Tag 0C0T only through that cover
  (Tag 0BUT). For `V = Y` this is descent along `f` with `f_* 𝒪_X = 𝒪_Y`.
* `Stacks.PicFinite.exists_isInvertible_modulePullback_iso_of_hasTrivializingTargetCover`: its
  case of a morphism which is an isomorphism over `V`.

## Implementation notes

**Which `IsInvertible`.** The construction runs in `Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible`, the
class in which Tag 0BUT and the gluing step are stated. Tag 0C0T itself is stated in the
definitionally identical `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible`, the class of Tag 01CS;
the two are crossed once, by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_iff_algebraicGeometry`.

The index set of the cover is the carrier of `Y` itself, with `chart y` a neighbourhood of `y`;
this avoids threading a separate indexing type and makes the pairwise condition a statement
about two points.

